ain-density","release_id":"openai-math","schema":"statement-map-web/2","section":1,"section_title":"Introduction","source":{"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:06999fd2ffad09b9507429612dbb9254276e39ff4db326de472ed3ee65be7cf1","file":"preprints/Goldfelds-analytic-density-conjecture-and-the-2-converse-for-elliptic-curves-October-7-2026/build/sections/00-introduction.tex","line":35,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"8701576bfceae4883675d0efdd68f275f636d2601e76dcf2a9d0ae86307f1e72","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Goldfelds-analytic-density-conjecture-and-the-2-converse-for-elliptic-curves-October-7-2026/build/sections/00-introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:06999fd2ffad09b9507429612dbb9254276e39ff4db326de472ed3ee65be7cf1","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Goldfelds-analytic-density-conjecture-and-the-2-converse-for-elliptic-curves-October-7-2026/build/sections/00-introduction.tex#L35"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:main-density}\nFor every elliptic curve $E/\\Q$ and each $j\\in\\{0,1\\}$,\n\\[\n \\lim_{X\\to\\infty}\n \\frac{\\#\\{d\\in\\mathcal D(X):a(E^{(d)})=j\\}}{\\#\\mathcal D(X)}\n =\\frac12.\n\\]\nConsequently the twists of analytic rank at least two have density zero.\nFor a density-one set of signed squarefree parameters $d$, the analytic\nand Mordell--Weil ranks of $E^{(d)}$ agree and its whole\nTate--Shafarevich group is finite."}
